<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.15.1: Analyzing Graphs that Represent Linear Equations and Inequalities</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00648</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.15.1: Analyzing Graphs that Represent Linear Equations and Inequalities</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a4765deb-0b32-4783-a057-43ab21190d1f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>

      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Compare each of the following graphs, then list a reason for each graph why it would not
        belong with the other three.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Graph A.</para>
        <media alt="Graph of two lines on a coordinate plane">
          <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_17_02_01.svg"/>
        </media>

    
      <para id="para-00003">Graph B.</para>
        <media alt="Graph of two inequalities on a coordinate plane">
          <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_17_02_02.svg"/>
        </media>

      <para id="para-00004">Graph C.</para>
        <media alt="Graph of two inequalities on a coordinate plane">
          <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_17_02_03.svg"/>
        </media>

      <para id="para-00005">Graph D.</para>
        <media alt="Graph of an inequality on a coordinate plane">
          <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_17_02_04.svg"/>
        </media>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00006">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00007">Your answers may vary,, but here are some samples.</para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>Graph A is the only set of graphs that represents a system of equations. It is the
              only system with exactly one solution.</item>
            <item>Graph B is the only set of graphs that represents a system of inequalities with no
              solutions.</item>
            <item>Graph C is the only set of graphs in which the boundaries are horizontal and
              vertical lines. It is the only one representing a system with an infinite number of
              solutions.</item>
            <item>Graph D is the only graph that does not represent a system. It only represents one
              inequality.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
